1
00:00:00,242 --> 00:00:02,622
Way to destroy your reputation.

2
00:00:03,578 --> 00:00:07,128
(Sheldon:)You see? People have been pointing
and laughing at me all morning.

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,830
It's not true.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
(Sheldon:)People have been pointing and laughing
at you your whole life.

5
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:14,800
(Sheldon:)All right, I've had enough.
Attention, everyone.

6
00:00:14,965 --> 00:00:16,635
I'm Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,090
(Sheldon:)As many of you
in the Physics Department know...

8
00:00:19,261 --> 00:00:21,851
(Sheldon:)...my career trajectory
has taken a minor detour.

9
00:00:22,013 --> 00:00:23,723
Off a cliff.

10
00:00:25,475 --> 00:00:28,315
(Sheldon:)-My credibility may have been damaged.
-Completely wrecked.

11
00:00:28,478 --> 00:00:33,228
(Sheldon:)But I would like to remind you that in
science there's no such thing as failure.

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,980
(Sheldon:)There once was a man...

13
00:00:35,152 --> 00:00:38,152
(Sheldon:)...who referred to his prediction
of a cosmological constant...

14
00:00:38,321 --> 00:00:40,571
(Sheldon:)...as the single biggest blunder
of his career.

15
00:00:40,741 --> 00:00:44,991
(Sheldon:)That man's name was, surprise, surprise,
Albert Einstein.

16
00:00:46,913 --> 00:00:49,163
Yeah, but research into dark energy
proved...

17
00:00:49,332 --> 00:00:52,462
...Einstein's cosmological constant
was actually right all along.

18
00:00:52,627 --> 00:00:59,027
So you're still, surprise, surprise,
a loser.

